mpegv.library: changes
======================

2.4 (16 November 2026)
----------------------

- MpvToRGBScaled's 16-bit formats on the 68k in one pass written by hand
  (src/convert_68k.s): each source pixel converted (three look-ups OR'd)
  and written as many times as the scaling needs, straight out, no row
  between; each chroma row's sums made once for its two rows. 720 x 576
  to 1024 x 576 RGB565: 54 M 68020 cycles (2.3: 74 M). The same bytes
  (tests/rgb_test.c, on a 68020).

2.3 (16 November 2026)
----------------------

- MpvToRGBScaled: a picture made RGB at another size as it is written,
  the nearest pixel, straight into a screen's bitmap in its own format:
  each source row it shows converted once into a row of fast memory (a
  chroma sample's sums once for its two pixels), then copied out to the
  output's columns. A DVD picture made 1024 x 576 RGB565: 74 million
  68020 cycles (vamos' count) where AmigaMCE's own conversion, a pixel
  at a time, took 158 million (56 ms under Amiberry's JIT, more than a
  picture's 40). Without memory for the row, a pixel at a time.
- MpvToRGB's formats (and MpvToRGBScaled's): MPVR_RGB555PC,
  MPVR_BGR565, MPVR_BGR565PC, MPVR_BGR555, MPVR_BGR555PC, so every 15-
  and 16-bit screen format is written directly.
- The 32-bit formats' alpha byte is written with the colours, not in a
  pass of its own first.
- tests/rgb_test.c: every format, at its size and scaled (larger,
  smaller, odd sizes), against a conversion a pixel at a time, on this
  computer and on a 68020.

2.2 (15 November 2026)
----------------------

- Times after MPVC_FLUSH: a picture's mpic_PTS was carried on from the
  last picture before the flush until one with its own came. A DVD times
  only its I pictures, so after a jump the new part's first B pictures
  (an open GOP's, shown before its I picture) had the old part's time:
  seconds off (Alien's language menu: 35.2 s for 0.08 s), and a player
  timing by them waited that long. Now nothing is carried across a
  flush, and a B picture shown before the first picture with a time
  (after a flush or at the start) is timed back from the I or P picture
  after it, by their temporal references: there, 0.080 and 0.120 s
  before the I picture's 0.160. The same at a stream's start (its first
  B pictures had no time at all).

2.1 (14 November 2026)
----------------------

- Faster, to leave a 68k's CPU room for AC-3 sound: 7-9% fewer cycles a
  picture (a PAL DVD's about 73 million, a VCD's about 10.6 million).
- The IDCT's columns are Arai, Agui and Nakajima's transform in 68k
  assembler (five multiplies, not eleven), its rows prescaled for it.
  No longer libmpeg2's to the bit: within IEEE 1180 (mean square error
  0.015 to libmpeg2's 0.013), 66 dB of luma PSNR on average against an
  exact decoder, as 2.0. Everything else is still libmpeg2's to the bit
  (make test builds 2.0's IDCT, MPEGV_EXACT_IDCT, to check it).
- A block's coefficients are decoded in 68k assembler, the bit buffer in
  registers across the block; the same as libmpeg2's C to the bit.
- third_party/libmpeg2/CHANGES has the details; README.md's Speed the
  cycles.

2.0 (14 November 2026)
----------------------

- The decoder is libmpeg2 0.5.1, not pl_mpeg: MPEG-2 (main profile,
  4:2:0, as on a DVD: interlaced, field pictures, 3:2 pulldown) as well
  as MPEG-1. Its pictures are libmpeg2's own, bit for bit; its IDCT does
  only what each block needs with 16-bit products (the column pass in
  68k assembler, MPEG-2's mismatch row from tables), its motion
  compensation works four pixels at a time (half-pel both ways reusing
  each row's sums), its bitstream is read a word at a time, its
  coefficients dequantised with 16-bit multiplies, its start codes
  sought four bytes at a time (third_party/libmpeg2/CHANGES).
- MpvToYUV422 and MpvToGrey are 68k loops (35% and 45% faster), MpvToRGB
  works from tables (RGB565 56% faster); the same bytes as before. MPEG-2 that is not 4:2:0 is
  refused (MPVE_FORMAT).
- The library's own Program Stream demultiplexer: MPEG-1 and MPEG-2 pack
  and PES headers, a DVD's VOB (private stream 1 with its substream,
  navigation packets passed to the packet hook, padding passed over). Each
  picture has its own time stamp (mpic_PTS), not the first one's plus its
  number's time.
- New: MpvExamine (MPEG-2, profile and level, interlace, the picture's
  shape as shown, the display extension); each picture's mpic_Duration,
  mpic_Fields and flags (top field first, repeated first field,
  progressive frame, field pictures); mpic_Time counts fields shown;
  mp_SubStream; MPVA_VideoStream; MPVC_FLUSH (after a seek).
- B pictures that need a picture the decoder has not had (an open GOP's
  first) and pictures before the first I picture are passed over, not
  shown as garbage.
- A bare video stream's last picture is no longer lost.
- Source-compatible with 1: MpvGetInfo fills only 1's fields, the
  structures the library hands out only grew at their ends.
- GPL-3.0-or-later (libmpeg2 is GPL-2.0-or-later); the interface and the
  example stay MIT. The Aminet archive no longer carries the source: it
  is at https://github.com/luvwagn/mpegv.library.
- A 68020's cycles a picture (vamos): a VCD's about 11.5 million, a PAL
  DVD's about 79 million (README.md's Speed).

1.0 (14 November 2026)
----------------------

- First release: pl_mpeg's MPEG-1 decoder and demultiplexer, made about
  2.6 times faster on a 68020. Made for Ambiance, an Amiga Media Center
  application.
